  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "2 Timothy",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "Paul describes the apostasy and perilous times of the last days—The scriptures guide man to salvation.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "This know also, that in the last days perilous times shall come.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Morm. 1:17 (13–17); 8:28 (26–33). TG Last Days."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "2 Tim. 4:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For men shall be lovers of their own selves, covetous, boasters, proud, blasphemers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "TG Covet."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Pride."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "TG Contention; Disobedience; Family, Children, Duties of."
          },
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "TG Ingratitude."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Without natural affection, trucebreakers, false accusers, incontinent, fierce, despisers of those that are good,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "Rom. 1:26 (26–28)."
          },
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Sexual Immorality."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Honesty."
          },
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "GR slanderers."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "GR without self-control."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Traitors, heady, highminded, lovers of pleasures more than lovers of God;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Rebellion."
          },
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "GR rash, reckless."
          },
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "GR puffed up, conceited."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Pleasure."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Having a form of godliness, but denying the power thereof: from such turn away.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Rom. 2:20; 2 Ne. 28:5; JS—H 1:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For of this sort are they which creep into houses, and lead captive silly women laden with sins, led away with divers lusts,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Woman."
          },
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "TG Lust."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ever learning, and never able to come to the knowledge of the truth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Learn."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Ignorance; Knowledge."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "TG Truth."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now as Jannes and Jambres withstood Moses, so do these also resist the truth: men of corrupt minds, reprobate concerning the faith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Opposition."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "Ps. 14:1; D&C 10:21 (20–23); 112:23 (23–24)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But they shall proceed no further: for their folly shall be manifest unto all men, as theirs also was.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "D&C 35:7; 45:49; 63:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But thou hast fully known my doctrine, manner of life, purpose, faith, longsuffering, charity, patience,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "GR followed closely, conformed to."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Persecutions, afflictions, which came unto me at Antioch, at Iconium, at Lystra; what persecutions I endured: but out of them all the Lord delivered me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "Acts 15:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 125
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, and all that will live godly in Christ Jesus shall suffer persecution.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Godliness."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "Ps. 34:19. TG Suffering."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "TG Cruelty; Persecution."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But evil men and seducers shall wax worse and worse, deceiving, and being deceived.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "GR diviners, imposters, cheats."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But continue thou in the things which thou hast learned and hast been assured of, knowing of whom thou hast learned them;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "D&C 66:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 121
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And that from a child thou hast known the holy scriptures, which are able to make thee wise unto salvation through faith which is in Christ Jesus.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Deut. 4:9 (6–9)."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Scriptures, Study of."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "TG Salvation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "JST 2 Tim. 3:16 And all scripture given by inspiration of God, is profitable …"
          },
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Book of Mormon; Scriptures, Writing of; Scriptures to Come Forth."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Inspiration."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "GR beneficial or useful for instruction."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "TG Scriptures, Value of."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Chastening; Reproof."
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "TG Education."
          },
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 139,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That the man of God may be perfect, throughly furnished unto all good works.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "GR suited, ready, complete. TG Perfection."
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Good Works."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
